  "description": "Twelve synthetic, disclosure-safe LabExportPacket/v1 build cases for the WP-I81 export-adversarial corpus. Every object here is SYNTHETIC: synthetic sha256 digests are LOW-ENTROPY (a 2-hex pattern repeated 32 times, Shannon entropy <= 1.0 bits/char) so the secret_scan long_hex detector does not flag them, while remaining valid 'sha256:<64 hex>' identities; disclosure-safe summaries describe the science (never the environment). No local paths, no credentials, no private keys, no raw dataset markers, no T7/VPS topology identifiers, no live/trading/promotion flags, no argv/shell markers, no env assignments. The corpus covers the coarse object-type vocabulary (claim, math_ir, receipt, catalog, evidence, plan, request, pilot, condition, constant, model interface, adapter, symbol table) AND BOTH disclosure policies (digest_replaced and omitted), single-object and multi-object packets, empty and non-empty provenance, both default and tightened summary_max_bytes budgets. The WP-I81 gate (scripts/checks/wp81-corpus.py) rebuilds each case through srl.bridge.exporter.build_packet and asserts it builds, schema-validates, and is under the 1 MiB cap. This file is scanner-clean under scripts/checks/public_boundary.py and scripts/checks/secret_scan.py EVEN WHEN TRACKED.",
